00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.420
and if they can even do that,

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.590
I'm about to take a deep dive

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.810
into the ironclad case against Flynn,

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.550
and the ins and outs
of 18 USC Section 1001,

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.990
and the big mess at the
Department of Justice.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.290
Let's start with some
background on Michael Flynn,

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.410
and how he found himself in
this particular situation.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.760
Michael Flynn was only employed
by the Trump administration

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.860
for 24 days,

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.990
but a lot happened during those 24 days.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:41.440
Flynn made many phone calls
to foreign governments,

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:42.690
particularly to Russia,

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.340
and then lied to to the FBI,

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.820
and particularly the Trump administration,

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.120
about those phone calls.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.460
This happened during a period

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.350
when Flynn was already being investigated

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.120
for working with the Russians.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.630
So just who is Lieutenant
General Michael Flynn anyway?

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.450
Well before joining the
Trump administration,

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.560
Michael Flynn was a
retired Lieutenant General

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.080
who held two intelligence posts
with the Federal Government.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.220
Flynn was the Director of the
Defense Intelligence Agency

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:07.370
under President Obama,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.580
and served as the
National Security Advisor

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.663
to President Trump.

00:03:10.663 --> 00:03:12.740
While serving in the Obama Administration,

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:16.060
Flynn became the first American
to visit the GRU in Moscow.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.612
The GRU is the successor to the KGB.

00:03:18.612 --> 00:03:21.550
Flynn retired from the DIA in 2015,

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.320
a year earlier than expected,

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.870
and then scuttlebutt is
that Flynn's resignation

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:28.890
was generally attributed
to being a not-great boss.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.820
But Flynn's stints in
the intelligence world

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:32.270
were marred by allegations

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.990
of mishandling of sensitive information

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.470
and, potentially, deception.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:37.320
When a government official
serves in a position

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.690
where they handle sensitive information,

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.420
they are required to disclose all contacts

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.514
with foreign nationals and governments.

00:03:41.514 --> 00:03:43.991
During Flynn's time as DIA Chief,

00:03:43.991 --> 00:03:46.020
his activities raised alarms

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.470
among some CIA and British
Intelligence Officers.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.690
They claimed that Flynn
concealed his relationship

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.560
with a Russian-British graduate
student, Svetlana Lokhova,

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.208
whom Flynn met on a trip to
Cambridge in February of 2014.

00:03:56.208 --> 00:03:59.190
The two carried-on an
email correspondence,

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:01.700
with Flynn referring to
himself as "General Misha."

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.870
Now, there's no proof
that Lokhova was a spy

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.210
or a honey trap for Flynn,

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.370
and in fact she later
filed a defamation lawsuit

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.277
against "The Wall Street
Journal," "The New York Times,"

00:04:09.277 --> 00:04:11.239
"The Washington Post,"
and MSNBC, amongst others.

00:04:11.239 --> 00:04:14.450
And this will be of interest
to all of you Legal Eagles

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:15.990
who watch my videos about defamation,

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:19.240
because her lawyer was none
other than Steven Biss,

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:21.410
the same lawyer who represents Devin Nunes

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.830
in many of his,

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.180
what I think almost everyone agrees,

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.740
are frivolous defamation lawsuits

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.920
against Internet cows and
other phantom menaces.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.904
Now, Lokhova's case was dismissed.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.510
It was actually handled
by a friend of mine,

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.440
and I think this generally falls

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.690
into what you would
consider an anti-slapsuit.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.180
But one of the questions

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.570
that tangentially I would
like to have answered is,

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.210
who is paying for Steven Biss

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:47.010
to file all of these
crazy defamation lawsuits?

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.410
If you happen to know the
answer to that question,

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:49.600
please send me an email,

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.630
'cause I would very much like to know.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:52.463
At any rate,

00:04:52.463 --> 00:04:55.070
after Flynn's retirement
from the armed services,

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.620
and from the intelligence community,

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:57.920
he started a consulting business

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.400
called the Flynn Intel Group.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.620
And in 2016, Flynn
appeared at a conference,

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.320
whose participants
discussed the coup attempt

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.410
against Turkish dictator Recept Erdogan.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:06.380
And at the time,

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.930
Flynn was on record for
getting rid of Erdogan,

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:11.760
who he believed was pushing
Turkey away from secularism,

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.300
and toward radical Islam.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.950
- Really became a secular country,

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:18.471
meaning a sort of a regular
sort of nation state,

00:05:18.471 --> 00:05:21.280
and then began to move towards Islamism.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.440
This is Turkey.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.150
- You may recall that
Erdogan was the one that,

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:24.983
a few years ago,

00:05:24.983 --> 00:05:26.390
had his armed guards

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.415
beat the crap out of a bunch
of protestors here in DC.

00:05:29.415 --> 00:05:31.636
But, as so often happens,

00:05:31.636 --> 00:05:34.910
Turkish business groups
hired Flynn Intel Group,

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.770
and paid them lots of money,

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:40.560
such that by 2016 Flynn was
lobbying on Erdogan's behalf.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.580
And on Election Day in 2016,

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.310
Flynn wrote an op-ed for "The Hill"

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.522
explaining the US needed
to fully support Erdogan.

00:05:46.522 --> 00:05:48.570
And this was a particularly big deal,

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.600
because Flynn was the
former Head of the DIA,

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.870
and was close to the incoming President.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.056
But there was one big problem:

00:05:55.056 --> 00:05:58.680
Flynn had failed to disclose
that he had be paid by Turkey

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.150
for the consulting work
when he wrote the op-ed.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.090
And, "The Hill" amended the article,

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.740
saying that Flynn didn't tell them

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.570
that his firm had received payments

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.040
from a company with close ties
to the Turkish government,

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.130
nor did he tell them

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.040
that the company had reviewed
the draft of the op-ed

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.610
before it was submitted.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:14.500
And, on top of that,

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.770
as a retired military
intelligence officer,

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.880
Flynn is required to
obtain prior permission

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.580
from the Defense Department
and the State Department

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.299
before receiving any money
from foreign governments.

00:06:23.299 --> 00:06:25.300
However, after Flynn retired,

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.240
he accepted $45,000 from "Russia Today,"

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.820
an English-language media outlet

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.587
that is owned by the Russian government.

00:06:31.587 --> 00:06:34.700
"Russia Today" paid Flynn
to attend a dinner in Moscow

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.190
where he hung out with none
other than Vladimir Putin

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.460
and the Green Party's own Jill Stein.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.100
Now, Flynn also accepted money
from Kremlin-linked companies

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.170
for speaking engagements,

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.710
but again, he didn't seek
approval for any of this.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.510
And this is where FARA
comes in for the first time.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.810
After it was clear that
Flynn was deeply involved

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.530
in promoting Erdogan's interests,

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.170
this caught the attention of the Pentagon

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.140
and other intelligence
services around the world.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:56.973
It was clear

00:06:56.973 --> 00:06:58.530
that Flynn's secret work
for foreign governments

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:01.000
may have violated the Foreign
Agents Registration Act,

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:01.860
or FARA.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.498
FARA is a law that requires individuals

00:07:03.498 --> 00:07:05.779
who are representing political
interests of foreign powers

00:07:05.779 --> 00:07:08.940
disclose their relationship
with the foreign government,

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:12.290
and the information related
to activities and finances.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.123
In other words,

00:07:13.123 --> 00:07:14.330
if you're working for foreign governments,

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.360
the American public has
a right to know about it.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.180
This is obviously particularly important

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:21.180
where there are major policy
differences between countries.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:22.353
And in this particular case,

00:07:22.353 --> 00:07:24.000
for the last five years,

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.700
the United States and
Turkey have disagreed

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:28.550
over where the US should
extradite Fethullah Gulen,

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.680
a Muslim cleric

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.780
living in the mountains
of eastern Pennsylvania.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.030
Gulen, who's 81,

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.620
is the leader of a religious movement

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.730
within Sunni Islam called Hizmet.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:38.740
Some say promote peace and civility,

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.300
whereas Erdogan believes
that Gulen is a terrorist

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:44.130
who is behind efforts to
remove him from power.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:44.980
Now, at the same time,

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.080
a Turkish national named Bijan Rafiekian

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.460
was a partner in the Flynn Intel Group.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.900
Rafiekian, Flynn, and others
lobbied the US government

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.680
to extradite Gulen to Turkey.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.950
And as it happens, Rafiekian
and a co-conspirator,

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.750
were later convicted in their role

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.420
in plotting to covertly influence

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:02.980
United States politicians and
public opinion against Gulen.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:04.470
And, as if this wasn't enough,

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.560
Flynn and his son were
allegedly offered $15 million

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.090
to travel to the Poconos and kidnap Gulen

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.920
and extradite him to Turkey.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.920
And, a reminder why this is important,

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.180
Flynn was frequently
lobbying foreign governments

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.180
without disclosing his activities
or his pay arrangements.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.454
And it was around the same time that,

00:08:20.454 --> 00:08:24.020
despite this activity,
or perhaps because of it,

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.690
Donald Trump tapped Michael Flynn

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:27.490
to be his National Security Advisor.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:30.148
Now, because of this, on August 16, 2016,

00:08:30.148 --> 00:08:31.747
the FBI opened up an investigation

00:08:31.747 --> 00:08:33.460
to find out whether Flynn

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:36.080
was being controlled or
influenced by Russia.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.840
He was being investigated
for violating 18 USC 951,

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.080
which makes it illegal
to be a foreign agent.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:45.410
This investigation wound-down
by January 4, 2017,

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.410
right before Donald Trump took office.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.570
The FBI was preparing to close this case.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.300
However, during the same period,

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.130
the Obama administration
was trying to understand

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.209
why Russia had not responded
to the additional sanctions

00:08:56.209 --> 00:08:58.530
that they had levied against Russia

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.910
for hacking US elections.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:03.760
What they learned is that Flynn
had actually been chatting

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.530
with Russian Ambassador Kislyak.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:07.760
Now, there are some circumstances

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.807
where you might want to
talk to a foreign colleague

00:09:11.807 --> 00:09:12.640
for various reasons,

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:14.420
and in transition situation.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.870
But what the FBI found

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:18.850
is that Flynn had been
discussing the sanctions

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.100
that had been levied against Russia

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.720
by the Obama administration.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:25.440
And there are disputes about
whether this conversation

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.159
was about policy or not.

00:09:27.159 --> 00:09:29.447
But the context of this conversation

00:09:29.447 --> 00:09:31.600
was that if Russia, indeed,

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:34.770
reacts against the Obama sanctions,

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:36.490
then effectively the Trump administration

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.210
is going to have to respond

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.650
once it takes office.

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:40.600
So the Trump administration

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.760
didn't want to be in a hole against Russia

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.610
and have to retaliate against it,

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:48.230
which, under any
reasonable interpretation,

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:50.810
is a conversation about policy.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:52.940
Now, the case agent in charge argued

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.360
that the Flynn investigation
should remain open

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.200
because of this particular information.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.800
Now, while the DOJ and the FBI

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:01.190
tried to figure out what to do,

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:02.860
Vice President Mike Pence

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:04.771
suddenly and publicly said that, in fact,

00:10:04.771 --> 00:10:07.960
Flynn did not interfere with the Russians,

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.570
and did not have policy
discussions about the sanctions.

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:13.660
Allegedly, that's because
Flynn lied to Mike Pence.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.180
Now, query whether Mike Pence

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:16.657
knew about this information or not,

00:10:16.657 --> 00:10:19.610
but the party line is
that Flynn lied to Pence,

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.480
Pence went public with the lie,

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.314
and by proxy,

00:10:23.314 --> 00:10:25.730
carried that misrepresentation forward

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:26.670
to the American public.

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.070
- I knew that he lied to me.

00:10:30.492 --> 00:10:32.442
And I know the President
made the right decision

00:10:32.442 --> 00:10:34.580
with regard to him.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.275
- And at that point the FBI
decided to interview Flynn

00:10:36.275 --> 00:10:39.679
about whether he was working
with the Russians or not.

00:10:39.679 --> 00:10:42.470
The interview wasn't about
election interference per se,

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:44.620
but it was in connection
with the ongoing concern

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.710
about Flynn's own actions.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:47.550
And, eventually,

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:51.958
Flynn agreed to have a voluntary
conversation with the FBI.

00:10:51.958 --> 00:10:53.410
So, in this context,

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:54.830
let's talk about the crime

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.356
of lying to the federal government.

00:10:56.356 --> 00:10:58.529
Under 18 USC 1001,

00:10:58.529 --> 00:11:00.920
it should surprise no
one that it is a crime

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.510
to lie to the federal government.

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:05.730
Section 1001 makes it a crime
to knowingly and willfully

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:07.740
make any materially false, fictitious,

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:08.770
or fraudulent statement,

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.090
or representation,

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:11.960
in any matter within the jurisdiction

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:13.797
of the executive legislative
or judicial branch

00:11:13.797 --> 00:11:14.940
of the United States.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:18.330
Now, to prove a violation of Section 1001,

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:20.539
the prosecutor must prove
the following five elements.

00:11:20.539 --> 00:11:23.120
Number one, a statement or representation,

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.688
or document was made or used.

00:11:24.688 --> 00:11:27.531
Two, it was false,
fictitious, or fraudulent.

00:11:27.531 --> 00:11:29.019
Three, it was material.

00:11:29.019 --> 00:11:31.959
Four, it was made or used
knowingly and willfully.

00:11:31.959 --> 00:11:34.670
And five, it was related to an action

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:36.805
within the authority of the
relevant federal agency.

00:11:36.805 --> 00:11:38.570
Now, the third element,

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:40.210
that a statement was material,

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.900
is often the most disputed issue

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:42.922
in a Section 1001 case.

00:11:42.922 --> 00:11:46.160
Now, according to the DOJ's own handbook,

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.590
the test for materiality
under Section 1001

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:50.130
is not whether a false statement

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:52.373
actually influenced a
government employee or function,

00:11:52.373 --> 00:11:55.859
but whether it had the
capacity to influence them.

00:11:55.859 --> 00:11:58.800
The ultimate issue, according to the DOJ,

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.360
is that if a lie is an attempts

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:01.970
to influence a decision-maker,

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:03.730
ie, convince them of something,

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:04.930
then it's material.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:05.780
It doesn't matter

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:08.220
if the FBI already
knows that you're lying,

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.500
or isn't convinced by your lie.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:13.365
That doesn't effect the
materiality of the lie itself.

00:12:13.365 --> 00:12:14.410
In other words,

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:16.880
it's not necessary to show
that the particular lie

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.480
ever really influenced anyone.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:20.469
And when the DOJ prosecuted Flynn,

00:12:20.469 --> 00:12:22.560
they argued, and the judge found,

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.767
that his lies were in fact material.

00:12:24.767 --> 00:12:26.480
So let's talk about the things

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.420
that Michael Flynn actually lied about.

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:29.680
In order to plead guilty,

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:33.314
Flynn had to agree to a detailed
statement of the offense.

00:12:33.314 --> 00:12:34.430
Now, this document

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.730
is not always a take-it
or leave-it proposition

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:37.760
from the prosecutors.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.269
In most cases, and certainly in this case,

00:12:39.269 --> 00:12:42.900
the defendant and lawyers
pour over the language,

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.710
and negotiate with the prosecutors,

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:47.730
about precisely what the
defendant is admitting to.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.950
So, what did Flynn admit to lying about?

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:52.170
Well, there are three categories of lies.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.570
First, lies regarding his communications

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:56.560
with the Russian Ambassador
to the United States.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:59.490
Second, lies about his
communications with Russia

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:01.160
and other countries about Israel.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:04.324
And third, lies about his paid
work for foreign governments.

00:13:04.324 --> 00:13:06.153
So let's talk about the
first category of lies,

00:13:06.153 --> 00:13:07.560
lies about Russia.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.140
The Special Counsel,
led by Robert Mueller,

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.460
was investigating Russia's role

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.540
in 2016 election interference.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:14.830
Now, a key issue was
whether the Trump campaign,

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.020
through intermediaries,

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.800
including Michael Cohen and Michael Flynn,

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:20.050
family members like Jared
Kushner and Don Jr.,

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:21.950
and campaign staff like Paul Manafort,

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.860
discussed the possibility of
lifting US sanctions on Russia

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:27.320
in exchange for help in the 2016 election.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.090
After President Trump was elected,

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:30.360
but before he was sworn-in,

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:31.193
the US government

00:13:31.193 --> 00:13:33.230
implemented additional
sanctions on Russia.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:35.190
Mueller reported that
people close to Trump

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.230
indeed tried to undermine US sanctions

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.697
before Trump was inaugurated.

00:13:38.697 --> 00:13:40.980
Now, according to Flynn's
statement of the offense

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:42.076
on January 24, 2017,

00:13:42.076 --> 00:13:46.360
Flynn voluntarily agreed to
an interview with FBI agents.

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.590
He wasn't coerced into
having this interview,

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.231
he voluntarily agreed
to talk with FBI agents.

00:13:51.231 --> 00:13:53.030
Now, during this interview,

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:55.820
Flynn said that he did not
ask Russia's Ambassador

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:58.070
to refrain from responding

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:00.820
to the new Obama sanctions against Russia.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.197
And he also said that he, quote,

00:14:02.197 --> 00:14:04.477
"Did not remember a follow-up conversation

00:14:04.477 --> 00:14:05.947
"where the Russian Ambassador said

00:14:05.947 --> 00:14:08.207
"that Russia had chosen
to moderate its response

00:14:08.207 --> 00:14:12.750
"because, specifically, of its
communications with Flynn."

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:15.960
Now, those statements
were unequivocally false.

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:18.700
Flynn admitted that on the
same day that President Obama

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:20.000
had signed an executive order

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.690
imposing sanctions against Russia

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:24.393
for its interference in the
2016 Presidential Election,

00:14:24.393 --> 00:14:26.630
the Russian Ambassador called Flynn.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.890
And when Flynn said he didn't
remember the conversation,

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:30.550
that was a lie.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.210
And there were additional phone calls

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:34.333
between Flynn, the Trump
Transition Team, and Kislyak.

00:14:34.333 --> 00:14:35.340
Flynn admitted

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.469
that after he phoned Trump's
people at Mar-a-Lago,

00:14:37.469 --> 00:14:39.620
he then called Ambassador Kislyak

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:42.190
to ask that Russia not
escalate the situation,

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.060
and only respond to the US sanctions

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.690
in a reciprocal manner.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:47.440
Flynn then reported back to the group

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:48.840
hunkered-down at Mar-a-Lago.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:51.610
Flynn spoke with Kislyak
again on December 31st,

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:54.127
when they discussed Russia's
intention not to retaliate

00:14:54.127 --> 00:14:55.847
in response to US sanctions,

00:14:55.847 --> 00:14:58.030
because of Flynn's request.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:58.870
And once again,

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.390
Flynn called senior members

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:02.060
of the presidential transition team,

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:04.960
to tell them that Russia
wasn't going to retaliate.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.550
Now, why does all of this matter?

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.001
Why are these lies material?

00:15:08.001 --> 00:15:11.130
Because Flynn was
communicating with Russia,

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:12.170
a foreign adversary,

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.710
that they didn't need to retaliate

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:15.490
against President Obama's sanctions,

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:16.913
leading to an inference
that he was telling them

00:15:16.913 --> 00:15:19.322
that President Trump would
get rid of the sanctions

00:15:19.322 --> 00:15:22.190
as soon as he was in a position to do so.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:24.222
It's also a signal that
President Trump didn't care

00:15:24.222 --> 00:15:27.249
that Russia, according to
intelligence agencies in the US,

00:15:27.249 --> 00:15:29.650
interfered in the US election.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.980
And perhaps most importantly,
and most shockingly,

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.970
the Russians, of course, knew at all times

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:36.910
what had and had not been
discussed with Michael Flynn,

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.424
and they knew what policy

00:15:38.424 --> 00:15:40.670
might and might not be on the table.

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:43.740
They knew what potential policy
changes were going to happen

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:45.220
with the Trump administration.

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:48.550
And worst of all, they had
caught Michael Flynn in a lie.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.810
They knew that Michael Flynn

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:52.180
had lied to Vice President Mike Pence,

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.470
and to the American people.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.440
So they now had leverage

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:58.753
against the National Security
Advisor to the United States.

00:15:58.753 --> 00:16:01.095
They knew that he had lied
to the American people.

00:16:01.095 --> 00:16:03.110
That's really bad.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:07.256
Apart from all of the legal
issues in Section 1001 or FARA,

00:16:07.256 --> 00:16:09.259
that's basically a worst-case scenario

00:16:09.259 --> 00:16:11.177
from a counterintelligence perspective.

00:16:11.177 --> 00:16:14.320
On top of that, there were
lies about a UN resolution.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.480
Michael Flynn admitted to
making false statements

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:18.222
about a UN Security Council resolution

00:16:18.222 --> 00:16:20.210
condemning Israeli settlements.

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:21.900
Flynn claimed that he did not request

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:22.840
that any of the countries

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.060
take any particular
action on the resolution.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:26.920
But, in his statement of the offense,

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:29.790
Flynn acknowledged that
the statement was false,

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:31.710
he really did contact the countries

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.650
to try and influence their vote in the UN.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.070
And then, there's the
third category of lies,

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:37.850
lies about paid work
for foreign governments.

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.830
When Michael Flynn took the
job with President Trump,

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:42.240
he made false statements

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:44.690
about what the Flynn Intel
Group had been up to.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.957
Specifically his activities, quote,

00:16:46.957 --> 00:16:49.206
"For the principle benefit
of the Republic of Turkey."

00:16:49.206 --> 00:16:50.867
Flynn made, quote,

00:16:50.867 --> 00:16:53.650
"Materially false statement
and omissions," end quote,

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:55.420
including hiding that
the Government of Turkey

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.230
was directing his activities.

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:59.460
Although Mueller did not
formally charge Flynn

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:00.710
with violating FARA,

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:03.543
he did include admissions
in the Statement of Offense,

00:17:03.543 --> 00:17:06.650
and Flynn has pled
guilty to those offenses.

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:09.060
So, that takes us to Flynn's guilty plea.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.440
So why did Flynn plead guilty?

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:13.640
Well, as with most criminals,

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.960
it's because cooperation
gets you a lighter sentence,

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:18.560
and sometimes being charged

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.188
with only a small fraction of the offenses

00:17:20.188 --> 00:17:23.260
that ultimately could
have come down the pike.

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:25.530
And Flynn decided to cooperate fully

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:26.863
with the Special Counsel's investigation.

00:17:26.863 --> 00:17:29.280
He participated in 19 interviews

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:30.830
with the Special Counsel's Office.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.940
And the extensive cooperation
convinced Robert Mueller

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:35.520
to recommend a relatively light sentence.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.190
And back in December 2017,

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:40.120
Flynn appeared in court
to enter his guilty plea.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.457
He did not object to the
prosecutor's description

00:17:42.457 --> 00:17:44.550
of his lies to the FBI.

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:47.300
And Flynn admitted that
he had violated the law.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:49.477
The judge asked, "Are you
entering this plea of guilty

00:17:49.477 --> 00:17:50.327
"because you are guilty,

00:17:50.327 --> 00:17:51.420
"and for no other reason?"

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:54.210
To which Flynn replied, "Yes, your honor."

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.190
He reaffirmed his plea at another hearing

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:57.840
on December 18, 2018,

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.870
one year after his first appearance,

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:01.436
and he said that he was satisfied

00:18:01.436 --> 00:18:03.170
with his lawyer's representations,

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:06.470
did not want a second opinion
about pleading guilty,

00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:08.280
and did not want to withdraw his plea

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:10.240
in light of certain FBI agents

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:12.040
being investigated for misconduct.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:15.580
And, that he knew lying to
the FBI was a federal crime.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:16.940
As part of that plea,

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:18.560
Flynn agreed not to file a motion

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:20.030
to withdraw his guilty plea.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.180
And although generally,

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:22.620
Federal Rule of Evidence 410

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.820
prohibits the use of
guilty plea statements

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:26.908
to incriminate a defendant
in later proceedings,

00:18:26.908 --> 00:18:29.478
Flynn explicitly waived
Rule 410 in his guilty plea.

00:18:29.478 --> 00:18:33.420
But by January of 2020,
Flynn had new lawyers.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.430
He had attempted to withdraw his plea,

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:37.380
and claim that all of
his earlier admissions

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.580
were actually lies,

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.120
and was asserting that he, in fact,

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.560
never lied to the FBI.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:43.490
Now that's not to say
that Flynn's prosecution

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:45.030
has been completely without issue.

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:46.600
Flynn has long complained

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:49.550
that he was being railroaded
by the deep state,

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:51.390
and he had long complained
that his lawyers

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:53.808
had a conflict of interest and
provided ineffective counsel.

00:18:53.808 --> 00:18:56.010
And that had largely been an issue

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:58.190
in terms of trying to
undo his guilty plea.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:01.410
He obviously had pleaded
guilty several times,

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:04.760
and was trying to be able
to withdraw that plea.

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.930
Now through most of this ordeal,

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:07.520
Flynn was represented by a firm

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:08.830
called Covington and Burling,

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.668
a huge US firm, white shoe,

00:19:10.668 --> 00:19:13.460
well-known for being
politically connected,

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:14.610
and one of the biggest

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:17.400
and most well-respected
firms in the country.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:18.970
Flynn dropped Covington and Burling

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.290
for the aforementioned reasons last year,

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:23.670
and signed with another
very well-known attorney

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:24.975
named Sidney Powell.

00:19:24.975 --> 00:19:28.090
Interestingly, in April
of 2020, of this year,

00:19:28.090 --> 00:19:29.420
Covington and Burling revealed

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:31.315
that they had recently uncovered emails

00:19:31.315 --> 00:19:34.330
and handwritten notes that they claimed

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.022
were inadvertently left
out of a trove of records

00:19:36.022 --> 00:19:39.190
that they turned over
to Flynn's new lawyer,

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.070
Sidney Powell.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:42.680
Now, it's hard to opine on the claims

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:43.850
of an effectiveness of counsel

00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:45.993
without knowing more about
the representation here.

00:19:45.993 --> 00:19:49.280
Ineffectiveness of counsel
is generally a defense

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:50.550
that applies to the indigent,

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:51.890
not a political appointee

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:53.600
with one of the biggest
firms in the country.

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:54.433
That said,

00:19:54.433 --> 00:19:56.440
it's pretty unusual to
have to turn over documents

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:59.270
long after you have
been fired by a client,

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:01.890
and have that client
retain another lawyer.

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:02.900
I mean, it's not a good look

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:05.270
to have potentially relevant documents

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:06.756
that the new attorney needs

00:20:06.756 --> 00:20:09.600
to review and to see.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:10.640
That being said,

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:12.079
Covington and Burling had these documents

00:20:12.079 --> 00:20:14.764
throughout their representation of Flynn,

00:20:14.764 --> 00:20:17.840
so it's a very hard burden to show

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.730
that failing to turn over these
documents to the new lawyer

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.770
is going to have prejudice
to the prior representation.

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:27.090
He's got a very steep
uphill climb to make there.

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:29.550
Which takes us to the actions
of the Department of Justice

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:32.780
under the guidance of
Attorney General Bill Barr.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.760
Now, with Flynn about to be sentenced,

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:36.290
there was speculation that President Trump

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.050
would actually pardon him for his crimes.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:41.160
But, it appears that instead,
Bill Barr took action.

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:43.030
First, in January 2020,

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:45.270
Barr appointed a US
attorney, Jeffrey Jensen,

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:47.100
to review Flynn's prosecution.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.270
This was unusual,

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:50.570
especially since Flynn
was about to be sentenced,

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:53.390
and Jensen had never reviewed
any of the prosecutions

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:56.060
that came from the Special
Counsel's investigation.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:21:00.700
And query why we have a
Special Counsel at all,

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.700
if the actions of the Special Counsel

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:05.190
can simply be reviewed and undone

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:07.380
by later Attorneys General.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:09.070
You can see that there might be a problem

00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:10.734
if you fire the Attorney General

00:21:10.734 --> 00:21:13.360
and then appoint an Attorney General

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:14.650
who's just going to undo

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:16.472
the supposedly independent investigations

00:21:16.472 --> 00:21:18.360
of the Special Counsel's Office.

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:19.320
We'll talk about that later.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.730
By the time that Jensen was
brought on to review the case,

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:23.290
the judge already ruled

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:25.630
that there was no reason
to dismiss the case.

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:26.870
But in a brand new motion,

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:29.240
the DOJ now claims that it
was totally inappropriate

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:31.470
for the FBI to question
Flynn in the first place,

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.940
and they're trying to dismiss
the claims against him,

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:36.080
despite his multiple guilty pleas,

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:38.200
and being on the eve of sentencing.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.610
And to sum that up,

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.840
Flynn was investigated
for being a Russian agent,

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:43.860
he had secretly talked to Russia

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.670
about undermining US sanctions,

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:48.350
he had lied to Mike Pence
about his involvement,

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:49.820
and whether that's legal or not,

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:51.460
it was the reason that Donald Trump gave

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:53.050
for firing Flynn in the first place,

00:21:53.050 --> 00:21:54.924
or at least leading to
Flynn's resignation.

00:21:54.924 --> 00:21:56.520
And he had a long history

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:58.686
of hiding his involvement
with foreign governments.

00:21:58.686 --> 00:22:00.030
Yet, unbelievably,

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:01.674
the DOJ is now saying that none of that

00:22:01.674 --> 00:22:04.840
was a good enough reason for
the FBI to interview Flynn,

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:06.341
and that those representations

00:22:06.341 --> 00:22:08.780
were not material to that investigation.

00:22:08.780 --> 00:22:11.460
And recall that the
Special Counsel's Office

00:22:11.460 --> 00:22:12.760
had a dual mandate.

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:14.760
They were both to investigate

00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:16.930
the counterintelligence issues at hand,

00:22:16.930 --> 00:22:19.510
and also any criminal
liability that might attach

00:22:19.510 --> 00:22:21.830
to the Russian hacking and interfering

00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:23.710
with the US Government.

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:27.770
Now, the only attorney to sign
the DOJ's motion to dismiss

00:22:27.770 --> 00:22:30.330
was newly appointed US
attorney Timothy Shea.

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:32.140
He's the head of the US Attorney's Office

00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:33.510
in the District of Columbia,

00:22:33.510 --> 00:22:35.409
and thus, he is one of the top three

00:22:35.409 --> 00:22:37.900
most powerful prosecutors in the country.

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:40.780
The other two being the
Southern District of New York

00:22:40.780 --> 00:22:43.240
and, arguably, the Eastern
District of Virginia.

00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:47.050
Potentially, the US Attorney's
Office for the District of DC

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:49.670
is the most powerful office;

00:22:49.670 --> 00:22:51.180
it depends on who you ask.

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:53.300
And it's important to note that Shea,

00:22:53.300 --> 00:22:56.000
who is a longtime colleague of Bill Barr,

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:59.300
replaces outgoing US attorney Jessie Liu,

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:02.075
who left the post at the
US Attorney's Office for DC

00:23:02.075 --> 00:23:04.600
to take up an appointed position

00:23:04.600 --> 00:23:06.150
with the Treasury Department.

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:07.550
But, just a few months ago,

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:08.876
the Trump administration

00:23:08.876 --> 00:23:11.664
inexplicably just removed
her nomination entirely,

00:23:11.664 --> 00:23:15.730
so she was effectively
fired from her past job.

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:18.100
And the Department of
Justice, through Timothy Shea,

00:23:18.100 --> 00:23:20.420
is arguing in this motion to dismiss,

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:21.253
that the government

00:23:21.253 --> 00:23:23.360
had already decided not to
charge Flynn under FARA,

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:25.700
so the decision to interview him

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:27.560
by the FBI was illegitimate.

00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:29.990
Now, the DOJ had not
officially written a memo

00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:31.150
closing the file.

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:33.860
But Shea portrays the
closure of the investigation

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:35.350
as a mere formality.

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:38.270
He went even further by
exonerating Flynn entirely,

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:41.870
stating that his chats with
Kislyak were totally fine.

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:43.601
And the DOJ's brand new position

00:23:43.601 --> 00:23:44.937
is that, quote,

00:23:44.937 --> 00:23:47.217
"There was no factual
basis for the predication

00:23:47.217 --> 00:23:49.152
"of a new counterintelligence
investigation,

00:23:49.152 --> 00:23:52.047
"nor was there a justification, or need,

00:23:52.047 --> 00:23:55.737
"to interview Mr. Flynn as to
his own personal recollections

00:23:55.737 --> 00:23:56.920
"of what had been said."

00:23:56.920 --> 00:23:59.460
The DOJ motion relies
heavily on an interview

00:23:59.460 --> 00:24:01.406
with former DOJ lawyer Mary McCord.

00:24:01.406 --> 00:24:04.189
This 2017 interview with McCord

00:24:04.189 --> 00:24:07.067
about the circumstances
of the investigation,

00:24:07.067 --> 00:24:10.250
was cited more than 25
times in the motion.

00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:13.950
However, Mary McCord wrote an
editorial just a few days ago,

00:24:13.950 --> 00:24:16.190
slamming her former employer, the DOJ,

00:24:16.190 --> 00:24:18.210
for twisting her own words.

00:24:18.210 --> 00:24:19.270
Now, although Mary McCord

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:21.100
is no longer with the
Department of Justice,

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:23.500
she was an incredibly
high-ranking official

00:24:23.500 --> 00:24:25.620
at the time of the Flynn investigation.

00:24:25.620 --> 00:24:26.453
She was, in fact,

00:24:26.453 --> 00:24:27.580
the Deputy Attorney General

00:24:27.580 --> 00:24:29.394
in charge of national security.

00:24:29.394 --> 00:24:30.741
According to McCord,

00:24:30.741 --> 00:24:33.617
her interview merely describes a, quote,

00:24:33.617 --> 00:24:35.687
"Difference of opinion about what to do

00:24:35.687 --> 00:24:36.937
"with the information that Flynn

00:24:36.937 --> 00:24:40.745
"apparently had lied to incoming
Vice President Mike Pence,"

00:24:40.745 --> 00:24:43.470
and whether Flynn's lies should be shared

00:24:43.470 --> 00:24:45.180
with President-elect Trump,

00:24:45.180 --> 00:24:47.060
not as to whether the investigation

00:24:47.060 --> 00:24:49.310
should proceed in the first place.

00:24:49.310 --> 00:24:50.750
McCord states that the debate

00:24:50.750 --> 00:24:52.500
was a completely different topic

00:24:52.500 --> 00:24:54.190
that had nothing to do with the legitimacy

00:24:54.190 --> 00:24:56.170
of interviewing Flynn.

00:24:56.170 --> 00:24:57.887
Quote, "The report of my interview

00:24:57.887 --> 00:25:00.353
"is no support for Mr. Barr's
dismissal of the Flynn case.

00:25:00.353 --> 00:25:02.627
"It does not suggest that the FBI

00:25:02.627 --> 00:25:04.587
"had no counterintelligence reason

00:25:04.587 --> 00:25:06.127
"for investigating Mr. Flynn.

00:25:06.127 --> 00:25:08.584
"It does not suggest that the
FBI's interview or Mr. Flynn,

00:25:08.584 --> 00:25:11.487
"which led to the false statements charge,

00:25:11.487 --> 00:25:12.939
"was unlawful or unjustified."

00:25:12.939 --> 00:25:15.733
McCord said that Flynn's
lies were material

00:25:15.733 --> 00:25:18.110
to a counterintelligence threat,

00:25:18.110 --> 00:25:21.460
because his lies exposed him
to the threat of blackmail.

00:25:21.460 --> 00:25:22.730
And McCord implies

00:25:22.730 --> 00:25:25.130
that the DOJ's new
arguments are misleading,

00:25:25.130 --> 00:25:27.540
because they ignore that the investigation

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:30.800
was into whether Flynn
had violated 18 USC 1951;

00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:31.633
in other words,

00:25:31.633 --> 00:25:33.316
whether he was actually
working with Russia or not.

00:25:33.316 --> 00:25:35.435
The official investigation was not closed,

00:25:35.435 --> 00:25:36.830
because the FBI learned

00:25:36.830 --> 00:25:38.700
about Flynn's conversations with Kislyak,

00:25:38.700 --> 00:25:40.390
and sought more information.

00:25:40.390 --> 00:25:41.326
I'm not an FBI agent,

00:25:41.326 --> 00:25:43.580
but it doesn't seem unreasonable

00:25:43.580 --> 00:25:45.780
for the FBI to hold
off on closing the file

00:25:45.780 --> 00:25:46.880
in order to question someone

00:25:46.880 --> 00:25:49.010
who might be spying for a foreign country.

00:25:49.010 --> 00:25:51.340
And DOJ prosecutors
originally told the court

00:25:51.340 --> 00:25:53.090
that Flynn's lies were material,

00:25:53.090 --> 00:25:55.380
and that any attempt to
undermine the sanctions

00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:56.910
could be evidence of collusion

00:25:56.910 --> 00:25:58.651
between Russia and the Trump campaign.

00:25:58.651 --> 00:26:01.880
Whether that ultimately
proved to be true or not

00:26:01.880 --> 00:26:03.720
doesn't mean that you can just get away

00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:05.448
with lying to the FBI with impunity.

00:26:05.448 --> 00:26:06.980
Again, it doesn't matter

00:26:06.980 --> 00:26:09.880
if the FBI believed what
you were saying at the time

00:26:09.880 --> 00:26:12.410
in order for the lies to be material.

00:26:12.410 --> 00:26:14.830
But in the motion that
was filed last week,

00:26:14.830 --> 00:26:16.480
the DOJ reversed itself,

00:26:16.480 --> 00:26:18.330
and ignored the judge's prior ruling,

00:26:18.330 --> 00:26:21.363
in order to claim that
things have simply changed.

00:26:21.363 --> 00:26:24.763
The DOJ hasn't really told
the court what that change is,

00:26:24.763 --> 00:26:26.440
it's just changing its position.

00:26:26.440 --> 00:26:29.530
And Tim Shea also argued that
the case should be dropped

00:26:29.530 --> 00:26:30.963
since the government
can't prove Flynn lied

00:26:30.963 --> 00:26:32.720
beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:35.390
This is particularly peculiar,

00:26:35.390 --> 00:26:36.840
given the number of times

00:26:36.840 --> 00:26:39.071
that Flynn has already plead
guilty to the matter itself.

00:26:39.071 --> 00:26:41.410
There's really no question that he lied,

00:26:41.410 --> 00:26:44.340
it's only a question of whether
that was material or not.

00:26:44.340 --> 00:26:45.990
Now, Shea's motion also claims

00:26:45.990 --> 00:26:47.340
that it's based on new information,

00:26:47.340 --> 00:26:49.790
but McCord confirms
that the DOJ had access

00:26:49.790 --> 00:26:51.320
to all this information the whole time.

00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:52.480
And speaking of which,

00:26:52.480 --> 00:26:56.090
one of the high-ranking FBI
agents has also come forward,

00:26:56.090 --> 00:26:58.760
claiming that the Barr-led
DOJ interviewed him

00:26:58.760 --> 00:27:02.530
about his actions and notes
surrounding the Flynn interview,

00:27:02.530 --> 00:27:03.970
and failed to apprise the court

00:27:03.970 --> 00:27:05.440
of his testimony in evidence,

00:27:05.440 --> 00:27:08.240
which he claims was counter
to the DOJ's narrative

00:27:08.240 --> 00:27:10.580
in the Shea motion to dismiss.

00:27:10.580 --> 00:27:12.840
Apparently in preparation
for this motion to dismiss,

00:27:12.840 --> 00:27:14.560
the DOJ interviewed Bill Priestap,

00:27:14.560 --> 00:27:16.900
who was the former head of
FBI Counterintelligence,

00:27:16.900 --> 00:27:19.540
two days before making
their extraordinary request

00:27:19.540 --> 00:27:21.610
to drop the case in
front of Judge Sullivan.

00:27:21.610 --> 00:27:23.850
Now, apparently they
didn't tell Judge Sullivan

00:27:23.850 --> 00:27:25.850
about Mr. Priestap's interview,

00:27:25.850 --> 00:27:26.870
and that's a bad look,

00:27:26.870 --> 00:27:28.870
because generally lawyers have a duty

00:27:28.870 --> 00:27:30.380
to present negative evidence,

00:27:30.380 --> 00:27:31.720
or negative authority to a judge.

00:27:31.720 --> 00:27:33.900
You don't have to give it the light

00:27:33.900 --> 00:27:35.320
most-favoring the other side,

00:27:35.320 --> 00:27:37.124
but you do have to at least
acknowledge that it exists.

00:27:37.124 --> 00:27:39.780
And "The New York Times"
reports that the DOJ

00:27:39.780 --> 00:27:41.200
is claiming that they're in the process

00:27:41.200 --> 00:27:43.030
of writing up a report of
the Priestap interview,

00:27:43.030 --> 00:27:45.820
and will, in fact, file
that with the court.

00:27:45.820 --> 00:27:47.310
We'll see if that happens.

00:27:47.310 --> 00:27:48.670
Now, Priestap apparently says

00:27:48.670 --> 00:27:50.836
that the FBI was never
trying to lay a perjury trap,

00:27:50.836 --> 00:27:53.030
and claims that FBI officials

00:27:53.030 --> 00:27:54.030
were trying to do the right thing

00:27:54.030 --> 00:27:55.160
in questioning Mr. Flynn,

00:27:55.160 --> 00:27:57.008
and knew of no effort to set him up;

00:27:57.008 --> 00:27:59.120
media reports to the contrary.

00:27:59.120 --> 00:28:01.300
Meanwhile, not everyone at
the Department of Justice

00:28:01.300 --> 00:28:03.120
is just sitting idly by.

00:28:03.120 --> 00:28:04.130
Brandon Van Grack,

00:28:04.130 --> 00:28:05.570
who heads a unit responsible

00:28:05.570 --> 00:28:07.330
for prosecuting violations in FARA

00:28:07.330 --> 00:28:08.530
withdrew from the case,

00:28:08.530 --> 00:28:10.600
and from two others
where Flynn is a party.

00:28:10.600 --> 00:28:12.160
This tends to be what happens

00:28:12.160 --> 00:28:14.460
when a lawyers does not
stand behind the pleading

00:28:14.460 --> 00:28:15.810
that his boss wants him to file.

00:28:15.810 --> 00:28:17.701
We saw that in the Roger
Stone sentencing case,

00:28:17.701 --> 00:28:21.536
where four US attorneys
withdrew from the case

00:28:21.536 --> 00:28:26.210
because of what appeared
to be improper interference

00:28:26.210 --> 00:28:27.190
by AG Barr.

00:28:27.190 --> 00:28:29.591
And although the Attorney
General is a political appointee,

00:28:29.591 --> 00:28:32.333
the DOJ's overall law enforcement goals

00:28:32.333 --> 00:28:34.130
shouldn't be partisan.

00:28:34.130 --> 00:28:36.930
The vast majority of people
who work at the FBI and the DOJ

00:28:36.930 --> 00:28:38.130
will spend their careers working

00:28:38.130 --> 00:28:40.098
for both Republican and
Democratic administrations.

00:28:40.098 --> 00:28:41.370
This doesn't mean

00:28:41.370 --> 00:28:43.325
that the aren't entitled
to political opinions,

00:28:43.325 --> 00:28:47.020
but their opinions aren't
germane to their investigations,

00:28:47.020 --> 00:28:48.140
and it shouldn't interfere,

00:28:48.140 --> 00:28:50.680
whether they decide to
prosecute someone or not,

00:28:50.680 --> 00:28:54.330
or give special treatment to
other people in government.

00:28:54.330 --> 00:28:56.367
And in fact, former DOJ
lawyer Jonathan Kravis

00:28:56.367 --> 00:28:59.020
wrote in an editorial for
"The Washington Post,"

00:28:59.020 --> 00:29:00.308
revealing that he left the DOJ

00:29:00.308 --> 00:29:02.210
because of similar machinations

00:29:02.210 --> 00:29:03.694
involving the Roger Stone investigation.

00:29:03.694 --> 00:29:07.220
Kravis was especially offended
by Barr's earlier comments,

00:29:07.220 --> 00:29:08.466
criticizing prosecutors for their actions.

00:29:08.466 --> 00:29:10.280
And, as Kravis points out,

00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:12.290
career prosecutors and FBI agents

00:29:12.290 --> 00:29:13.960
aren't allowed to comment publicly

00:29:13.960 --> 00:29:15.380
about criminal investigations,

00:29:15.380 --> 00:29:17.606
nor can they respond
to their boss, AG Barr.

00:29:17.606 --> 00:29:18.917
Kravis wrote:

00:29:18.917 --> 00:29:20.757
"Department lawyers are ethically bound

00:29:20.757 --> 00:29:22.597
"to protect the confidences
of their client,

00:29:22.597 --> 00:29:23.727
"the US Government.

00:29:23.727 --> 00:29:26.337
"Barr's decision to excuse
himself from these obligations

00:29:26.337 --> 00:29:28.985
"and attack his own silenced
employees is alarming.

00:29:28.985 --> 00:29:31.057
"It sends an unmistakable message

00:29:31.057 --> 00:29:32.597
"to prosecutors and agents -

00:29:32.597 --> 00:29:33.827
"if the President demands,

00:29:33.827 --> 00:29:35.487
"we will throw you under the bus."

00:29:35.487 --> 00:29:37.710
And Kravis is not alone.

00:29:37.710 --> 00:29:38.790
More than 2,000

00:29:38.790 --> 00:29:40.602
former Department of
Justice employees agree.

00:29:40.602 --> 00:29:43.010
They published a statement condemning Barr

00:29:43.010 --> 00:29:44.870
and calling for his resignation,

00:29:44.870 --> 00:29:47.817
stating, "The Department's
action is extraordinarily rare,

00:29:47.817 --> 00:29:49.227
"if not unprecedented.

00:29:49.227 --> 00:29:51.311
"If any of us, or anyone
reading this statement,

00:29:51.311 --> 00:29:53.657
"who is not a friend of the President,

00:29:53.657 --> 00:29:55.527
"were to lie to federal investigators

00:29:55.527 --> 00:29:57.187
"in the course of a properly predicated

00:29:57.187 --> 00:29:58.857
"counterintelligence investigation,

00:29:58.857 --> 00:30:01.357
"and admit we did so under oath,

00:30:01.357 --> 00:30:03.300
"we would be prosecuted for it."

00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:04.667
They go on to say that,

00:30:04.667 --> 00:30:05.907
"We thus unequivocally

00:30:05.907 --> 00:30:08.047
"support the decision
of the career prosecutor

00:30:08.047 --> 00:30:09.537
"who withdrew from the Flynn case,

00:30:09.537 --> 00:30:11.367
"just as we supported the prosecutors

00:30:11.367 --> 00:30:13.217
"who withdrew from the Stone case.

00:30:13.217 --> 00:30:15.597
"They are upholding the
oath that we all took,

00:30:15.597 --> 00:30:17.087
"and we call on their colleagues

00:30:17.087 --> 00:30:18.923
"to continue to follow their example."

00:30:18.923 --> 00:30:20.210
Like Kravis,

00:30:20.210 --> 00:30:23.250
these ex-employees are
also extremely concerned

00:30:23.250 --> 00:30:25.296
about retaliation by Barr and Trump.

00:30:25.296 --> 00:30:26.467
Quote: "President Trump

00:30:26.467 --> 00:30:28.517
"accused the career
investigators and prosecutors

00:30:28.517 --> 00:30:29.961
"involved in the Flynn case of treason,

00:30:29.961 --> 00:30:33.033
"and threatened that they
should pay a big price.

00:30:33.033 --> 00:30:35.597
"It is incumbent upon the
other branches of government

00:30:35.597 --> 00:30:38.064
"to protect from retaliation
these public servants,

00:30:38.064 --> 00:30:39.887
"and any others who were targeted

00:30:39.887 --> 00:30:41.767
"for seeking to uphold
their oaths of office

00:30:41.767 --> 00:30:43.023
"and pursue justice."

00:30:43.023 --> 00:30:45.147
Kravis is just as skeptical of claims

00:30:45.147 --> 00:30:47.380
that the DOJ is acting in good faith.

00:30:47.380 --> 00:30:49.557
Quote: "If the Department truly acted

00:30:49.557 --> 00:30:51.971
"because of good-faith
commitments to legal positions,

00:30:51.971 --> 00:30:54.607
"then where is the evidence
of those commitments

00:30:54.607 --> 00:30:55.440
"in other cases

00:30:55.440 --> 00:30:57.417
"that do not involve
friends of the President?

00:30:57.417 --> 00:30:59.227
"Where are the narcotics cases

00:30:59.227 --> 00:31:01.211
"in which the Department has
filed a sentencing memorandum

00:31:01.211 --> 00:31:03.517
"overruling career prosecutors?

00:31:03.517 --> 00:31:05.247
"Where are the other
false-statements cases

00:31:05.247 --> 00:31:07.090
"dismissed after a guilty plea?"

00:31:07.090 --> 00:31:08.025
Speaking for myself,

00:31:08.025 --> 00:31:09.870
if we wanna have a conversation

00:31:09.870 --> 00:31:11.460
about criminal justice reform,

00:31:11.460 --> 00:31:14.324
and curtailing some of the FBI's power,

00:31:14.324 --> 00:31:19.324
or their ability to use the
broad mandate of Section 1001

00:31:19.370 --> 00:31:23.240
so that we can talk about
a more fair justice system,

00:31:23.240 --> 00:31:24.617
I'm all for that.

00:31:24.617 --> 00:31:26.750
And a whole bunch of other defense lawyers

00:31:26.750 --> 00:31:29.562
would love to be able to
remove some of the power

00:31:29.562 --> 00:31:31.350
that the federal government,

00:31:31.350 --> 00:31:32.412
or other investigators have

00:31:32.412 --> 00:31:34.400
when investigating people.

00:31:34.400 --> 00:31:36.310
But this isn't one of those cases.

00:31:36.310 --> 00:31:39.423
This isn't a case of
reforming the underlying law.

00:31:39.423 --> 00:31:41.750
It's a case of special treatment

00:31:41.750 --> 00:31:45.560
doled out to one of the
President's closest advisors.

00:31:45.560 --> 00:31:49.640
That is the exact opposite
of the rule of law.

00:31:49.640 --> 00:31:51.120
That's crony-capitalism.

00:31:51.120 --> 00:31:52.680
It's corruption.

00:31:52.680 --> 00:31:55.520
So many people who had
no frame of reference

00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:58.100
lashed out at some of the
tactics that the FBI used

00:31:58.100 --> 00:31:59.390
in this particular case,

00:31:59.390 --> 00:32:00.721
and were appalled.

00:32:00.721 --> 00:32:02.120
But the truth is

00:32:02.120 --> 00:32:05.180
the FBI has done similar
things in thousands,

00:32:05.180 --> 00:32:07.720
if not hundreds of
thousands of other cases.

00:32:07.720 --> 00:32:08.730
You wanna have a conversation

00:32:08.730 --> 00:32:10.900
about reforming some of those actions?

00:32:10.900 --> 00:32:12.340
Fine, I'm all for it.

00:32:12.340 --> 00:32:14.901
But the Michael Flynn
case is not the venue

00:32:14.901 --> 00:32:16.960
for criminal justice reform.

00:32:16.960 --> 00:32:19.960
It's just, simply, special
favors being doled out

00:32:19.960 --> 00:32:20.970
to friends of the President.

00:32:20.970 --> 00:32:23.250
The opposite of the rule of law.

00:32:23.250 --> 00:32:24.880
Flynn had every advantage.

00:32:24.880 --> 00:32:26.500
He was at the highest
echelons of government.

00:32:26.500 --> 00:32:27.660
He had the best lawyers,

00:32:27.660 --> 00:32:30.780
and he spoke to the FBI,
voluntarily, of his own accord,

00:32:30.780 --> 00:32:32.250
on advice of counsel.

00:32:32.250 --> 00:32:33.250
He wasn't railroaded,

00:32:33.250 --> 00:32:36.020
he wasn't entrapped by the government.

00:32:36.020 --> 00:32:38.010
You wanna talk about
criminal justice reform,

00:32:38.010 --> 00:32:38.843
let's do it.

00:32:38.843 --> 00:32:39.970
This is not that case.

00:32:39.970 --> 00:32:42.060
So let's talk about what's
going to happen next,

00:32:42.060 --> 00:32:43.669
and the judge's role.

00:32:43.669 --> 00:32:45.850
Judge Sullivan is the presiding judge,

00:32:45.850 --> 00:32:48.070
and the government has
asked Judge Sullivan,

00:32:48.070 --> 00:32:49.260
in Flynn's case,

00:32:49.260 --> 00:32:51.560
to drop the prosecution entirely.

00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:53.440
Sullivan is not required to do so,

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:56.710
under Rule 48a of the Federal
Rules of Criminal Procedure,

00:32:56.710 --> 00:32:58.790
a government motion to
dismiss an indictment,

00:32:58.790 --> 00:33:00.077
even after a guilty plea,

00:33:00.077 --> 00:33:02.250
requires what's called leave of court.

00:33:02.250 --> 00:33:03.760
So the judge gets to decide.

00:33:03.760 --> 00:33:05.870
Judge Sullivan, probably,

00:33:05.870 --> 00:33:07.600
will grant the leave to dismiss,

00:33:07.600 --> 00:33:09.890
because there won't be an opposing party.

00:33:09.890 --> 00:33:11.410
Both the government and Flynn

00:33:11.410 --> 00:33:13.440
are going to argue in favor of dismissal.

00:33:13.440 --> 00:33:16.490
But Judge Sullivan does have
the discretion to deny it

00:33:16.490 --> 00:33:18.340
and just go straight to sentencing.

00:33:18.340 --> 00:33:21.240
And it's significant that
Flynn plead guilty twice,

00:33:21.240 --> 00:33:22.600
and that Judge Sullivan ruled

00:33:22.600 --> 00:33:25.200
Flynn's lies were material
to an investigation,

00:33:25.200 --> 00:33:27.940
and that he has already
received sentencing memoranda

00:33:27.940 --> 00:33:28.950
from both sides.

00:33:28.950 --> 00:33:31.340
But we don't really know
what Judge Sullivan will do.

00:33:31.340 --> 00:33:33.210
He's known as a mercurial judge,

00:33:33.210 --> 00:33:35.080
and he will go his own way.

00:33:35.080 --> 00:33:37.400
Okay, so fast forward a couple of days,

00:33:37.400 --> 00:33:40.410
and here's where things
really start to get crazy

00:33:40.410 --> 00:33:42.670
in terms of the prosecution
of Michael Flynn,

00:33:42.670 --> 00:33:45.040
and particularly, Judge Sullivan.

00:33:45.040 --> 00:33:47.570
So, in reaction to this, effectively,

00:33:47.570 --> 00:33:50.150
unprecedented motion by
the Department of Justice,

00:33:50.150 --> 00:33:52.270
Judge Sullivan started making some moves.

00:33:52.270 --> 00:33:54.105
The first thing that he
did, a couple of days ago,

00:33:54.105 --> 00:33:56.150
was that he issued a minute order,

00:33:56.150 --> 00:33:59.040
which is usually just a short
order that appears on PACER,

00:33:59.040 --> 00:34:00.945
have a huge document associated with it,

00:34:00.945 --> 00:34:03.539
in which he asked for third parties

00:34:03.539 --> 00:34:05.950
to write what's called an amicus brief.

00:34:05.950 --> 00:34:09.160
An amicus brief is a brief
filed by a third party

00:34:09.160 --> 00:34:12.540
that has no stake in the case itself.

00:34:12.540 --> 00:34:14.824
It's an amicus brief,
filed by an amicus curiae.

00:34:14.824 --> 00:34:19.270
And this is very, very
normal in an appeals context,

00:34:19.270 --> 00:34:22.080
where appeals cases have
far-reaching implications.

00:34:22.080 --> 00:34:23.130
They set precedent,

00:34:23.130 --> 00:34:25.820
and so it's not unusual for a third party

00:34:25.820 --> 00:34:26.850
to want to weigh in.

00:34:26.850 --> 00:34:29.620
When I have litigated in
front of the federal circuits,

00:34:29.620 --> 00:34:32.890
I often have third parties
file these amicus briefs,

00:34:32.890 --> 00:34:34.440
either in support of my arguments,

00:34:34.440 --> 00:34:35.719
or against my arguments,

00:34:35.719 --> 00:34:38.030
because they might be affected by it.

00:34:38.030 --> 00:34:41.500
An amicus brief is a very
unusual thing in a trial court,

00:34:41.500 --> 00:34:43.660
because generally nobody cares

00:34:43.660 --> 00:34:46.800
except the parties who
are actually in trial.

00:34:46.800 --> 00:34:49.200
But, court has inherent power

00:34:49.200 --> 00:34:51.466
to ask for these amicus briefs,

00:34:51.466 --> 00:34:54.930
and Judge Sullivan, here, has done so.

00:34:54.930 --> 00:34:58.140
He, apparently, wants additional opinions,

00:34:58.140 --> 00:35:00.120
or briefs, to be filed,

00:35:00.120 --> 00:35:01.628
about this particular situation.

00:35:01.628 --> 00:35:03.670
There are multiple ways of spinning this,

00:35:03.670 --> 00:35:05.090
but the most likely situation

00:35:05.090 --> 00:35:08.865
is that the judge is
showing his displeasure

00:35:08.865 --> 00:35:10.773
with the DOJ's position.

00:35:10.773 --> 00:35:12.990
That because there's no one arguing

00:35:12.990 --> 00:35:15.816
for the continued
prosecution of Michael Flynn,

00:35:15.816 --> 00:35:17.451
he wants a third perspective

00:35:17.451 --> 00:35:21.260
to be able to understand
countervailing issues.

00:35:21.260 --> 00:35:23.068
And given the unprecedented nature

00:35:23.068 --> 00:35:25.370
of this motion to dismiss,

00:35:25.370 --> 00:35:27.767
it's not crazy to want someone else

00:35:27.767 --> 00:35:31.700
going to bat for the
prosecution of Michael Flynn.

00:35:31.700 --> 00:35:32.550
Typically though,

00:35:32.550 --> 00:35:34.390
the federal judge usually accedes

00:35:34.390 --> 00:35:37.529
to the request of the DOJ prosecutors.

00:35:37.529 --> 00:35:40.740
If the DOJ doesn't want to move forward

00:35:40.740 --> 00:35:43.130
with the prosecution of an individual,

00:35:43.130 --> 00:35:45.370
generally there's no reason why the judge

00:35:45.370 --> 00:35:48.440
would not agree with that position.

00:35:48.440 --> 00:35:51.070
But obviously, for reasons
that we have already discussed,

00:35:51.070 --> 00:35:53.050
this is not a usual situation,

00:35:53.050 --> 00:35:57.700
and nothing is really normal
in the motion to dismiss

00:35:57.700 --> 00:35:59.370
that the DOJ has filed.

00:35:59.370 --> 00:36:02.907
Now, after Judge Sullivan
asked for these amicus briefs,

00:36:02.907 --> 00:36:05.258
that's when it really got real.

00:36:05.258 --> 00:36:07.964
He issued another order a few days later,

00:36:07.964 --> 00:36:12.640
in which Judge Sullivan has
asked for a magistrate judge

00:36:12.640 --> 00:36:16.070
to be appointed to basically
present an opposition

00:36:16.070 --> 00:36:17.764
to the DOJ's motion.

00:36:17.764 --> 00:36:21.330
The order seeks to appoint Judge Gleeson,

00:36:21.330 --> 00:36:23.280
who is a former federal prosecutor,

00:36:23.280 --> 00:36:24.781
and former federal judge,

00:36:24.781 --> 00:36:28.880
and that judge is going to, basically,

00:36:28.880 --> 00:36:31.110
make the arguments that
the DOJ is not making

00:36:31.110 --> 00:36:32.620
in moving forward with Michael Flynn.

00:36:32.620 --> 00:36:33.820
And on top of that,

00:36:33.820 --> 00:36:36.380
and here's where things
really get interesting,

00:36:36.380 --> 00:36:40.300
Magistrate Judge Gleeson
is going to decide

00:36:40.300 --> 00:36:43.120
if Michael Flynn has
committed criminal contempt

00:36:43.120 --> 00:36:44.192
by perjuring himself.

00:36:44.192 --> 00:36:46.010
So let's take a step back here,

00:36:46.010 --> 00:36:48.620
because this is pretty unprecedented.

00:36:48.620 --> 00:36:49.490
What is a magistrate?

00:36:49.490 --> 00:36:50.690
Well, a magistrate judge

00:36:50.690 --> 00:36:54.350
is sort of an ad hoc helper of the court.

00:36:54.350 --> 00:36:56.992
So the federal judges are all appointed

00:36:56.992 --> 00:36:59.210
by the President of the United States.

00:36:59.210 --> 00:37:02.080
And they often deal with situations

00:37:02.080 --> 00:37:03.770
that are either too complex,

00:37:03.770 --> 00:37:06.380
or too time consuming
to deal with themselves.

00:37:06.380 --> 00:37:09.640
Or, they want a neutral third party view

00:37:09.640 --> 00:37:11.260
on a particular issue.

00:37:11.260 --> 00:37:13.760
So you would create what's
called a magistrate judge,

00:37:13.760 --> 00:37:15.340
which is sort of an ad hoc position.

00:37:15.340 --> 00:37:16.960
I've run into magistrate judges a lot,

00:37:16.960 --> 00:37:18.310
because often judges

00:37:18.310 --> 00:37:19.770
don't want to have to deal with discovery,

00:37:19.770 --> 00:37:22.790
literally millions of pages of documents,

00:37:22.790 --> 00:37:24.780
and so they hand that off to a magistrate.

00:37:24.780 --> 00:37:27.573
Sometimes the magistrate
is a former federal judge,

00:37:27.573 --> 00:37:28.690
a retired federal judge,

00:37:28.690 --> 00:37:30.820
and sometimes it is a lawyer

00:37:30.820 --> 00:37:33.540
who wants to eventually become a judge;

00:37:33.540 --> 00:37:34.860
so they sort of get their training wheels

00:37:34.860 --> 00:37:36.270
by becoming a magistrate.

00:37:36.270 --> 00:37:37.350
In this particular case,

00:37:37.350 --> 00:37:41.230
Judge Gleeson is a former
federal judge, retired,

00:37:41.230 --> 00:37:43.440
but he's also a former federal prosecutor.

00:37:43.440 --> 00:37:48.030
And here, Judge Gleeson is
sort of wearing two hats.

00:37:48.030 --> 00:37:48.863
On the one hand,

00:37:48.863 --> 00:37:50.640
the first part of the order
requires Judge Gleeson

00:37:50.640 --> 00:37:54.200
to be an advocate to
oppose the DOJ's motion.

00:37:54.200 --> 00:37:55.670
And the second half of the order

00:37:55.670 --> 00:37:57.440
is effectively to be
a neutral third party,

00:37:57.440 --> 00:37:59.336
and make an independent decision

00:37:59.336 --> 00:38:00.950
as to whether Michael Flynn

00:38:00.950 --> 00:38:05.050
has committed criminal
contempt and perjured himself.

00:38:05.050 --> 00:38:06.530
Now, what's going to happen here

00:38:06.530 --> 00:38:08.600
is absolutely anyone's guess,

00:38:08.600 --> 00:38:10.670
and we don't really know what to expect,

00:38:10.670 --> 00:38:13.090
other than the fact that this question

00:38:13.090 --> 00:38:16.134
of whether Flynn committed
criminal contempt by perjury

00:38:16.134 --> 00:38:19.990
is separate from his 1001 guilty plea

00:38:19.990 --> 00:38:22.760
of lying to federal officials.

00:38:22.760 --> 00:38:23.720
So really,

00:38:23.720 --> 00:38:26.370
it can only be in connection
with the representations

00:38:26.370 --> 00:38:29.233
that Flynn has made to the court,

00:38:29.233 --> 00:38:30.112
and, of course,

00:38:30.112 --> 00:38:30.945
that is what criminal contempt is for.

00:38:30.945 --> 00:38:33.180
It's the inherent power of the judge

00:38:33.180 --> 00:38:35.170
to punish people for shenanigans

00:38:35.170 --> 00:38:37.170
that happen in front of them.

00:38:37.170 --> 00:38:38.003
Now of course,

00:38:38.003 --> 00:38:40.190
the DOJ dismissing a
case after a guilty plea

00:38:40.190 --> 00:38:41.830
is extraordinarily rate,

00:38:41.830 --> 00:38:43.940
to the point that I've
never heard of it happening,

00:38:43.940 --> 00:38:45.390
but the judge appointing a magistrate

00:38:45.390 --> 00:38:46.650
to oppose such a motion

00:38:46.650 --> 00:38:50.640
is just uncharted territory in general.

00:38:50.640 --> 00:38:51.860
Obviously some people are gonna argue

00:38:51.860 --> 00:38:53.360
that this is yet more evidence

00:38:53.360 --> 00:38:54.847
of the deep state
railroading Michael Flynn,

00:38:54.847 --> 00:38:56.559
and some are gonna argue

00:38:56.559 --> 00:38:58.110
that this is simply an independent judge

00:38:58.110 --> 00:39:02.270
standing up to a clearly inferior motion

00:39:02.270 --> 00:39:03.720
by the Department of Justice.

00:39:03.720 --> 00:39:07.500
But as with the request
for a third party briefing,

00:39:07.500 --> 00:39:09.990
this really signals that Judge Sullivan

00:39:09.990 --> 00:39:12.740
does not want to give into
the Department of Justice.

00:39:12.740 --> 00:39:13.620
He still might,

00:39:13.620 --> 00:39:16.650
but he's obviously going to
put the DOJ through the ringer

00:39:16.650 --> 00:39:17.780
before they get there.

00:39:17.780 --> 00:39:20.890
And, in fact, Sullivan has
actually done this before,

00:39:20.890 --> 00:39:23.100
with the prosecution of Ted Stevens.

00:39:23.100 --> 00:39:24.740
So, who knows what Judge Sullivan

00:39:24.740 --> 00:39:26.150
is ultimately going to do here.

00:39:26.150 --> 00:39:29.540
And not that the deep
state theory has any merit,

00:39:29.540 --> 00:39:31.290
but this may be, in fact,

00:39:31.290 --> 00:39:32.800
a bit of a whipsaw,

00:39:32.800 --> 00:39:35.000
that Judge Sullivan is taking out a stick

00:39:35.000 --> 00:39:37.850
to try to get Michael Flynn
to do things the easy way

00:39:37.850 --> 00:39:39.060
instead of the hard way.

00:39:39.060 --> 00:39:41.070
Judge Sullivan might be showing
that things can, in fact,

00:39:41.070 --> 00:39:42.550
get worse.

00:39:42.550 --> 00:39:45.570
That there's the possibility
of yet more jail time

00:39:45.570 --> 00:39:47.340
associated with criminal contempt,

00:39:47.340 --> 00:39:49.660
so it would behoove him
to simply move forward

00:39:49.660 --> 00:39:51.775
with the easy thing of the guilty plea,

00:39:51.775 --> 00:39:53.818
instead of making a ruckus

00:39:53.818 --> 00:39:57.340
and potentially finding more jail time.

00:39:57.340 --> 00:40:00.180
So it might be a reason
to persuade Michael Flynn

00:40:00.180 --> 00:40:03.020
to back down from the shenanigans

00:40:03.020 --> 00:40:05.800
and also try to get the DOJ to back down.

00:40:05.800 --> 00:40:08.301
Things can get worse before
they get better for them.

00:40:08.301 --> 00:40:11.410
But I'd say that the DOJ
has already been embarrassed

00:40:11.410 --> 00:40:12.380
by this whole episode,

00:40:12.380 --> 00:40:13.930
and it seems like things
are gonna get worse

00:40:13.930 --> 00:40:14.810
before they get better.

00:40:14.810 --> 00:40:15.890
But ultimately here,

00:40:15.890 --> 00:40:18.385
and this is great advice for
young lawyers, old lawyers,

00:40:18.385 --> 00:40:22.240
pretty much anyone that may
ever show up in federal court:

00:40:22.240 --> 00:40:24.430
do not mess with federal
judges (chuckling).

00:40:24.430 --> 00:40:26.010
They will make you regret that.

00:40:26.010 --> 00:40:28.800
So, it's anyone's guess
what may happen next.

00:40:28.800 --> 00:40:31.690
But this motion from the
Department of Justice

00:40:31.690 --> 00:40:35.710
is starting to create a
pattern from Bill Barr's DOJ.

00:40:35.710 --> 00:40:37.740
The DOJ is emboldened.

00:40:37.740 --> 00:40:41.610
It's suddenly contradicting
earlier prosecutorial decisions

00:40:41.610 --> 00:40:43.920
without any rationale or
change in circumstances,

00:40:43.920 --> 00:40:46.450
and career DOJ employees are resigning

00:40:46.450 --> 00:40:47.810
rather than sign the pleadings.

00:40:47.810 --> 00:40:50.730
Only Tim Shea signed
the motion to dismiss,

00:40:50.730 --> 00:40:53.280
and even then he did it
with the wrong bar number.

00:40:53.280 --> 00:40:56.110
And given the speculation
about a presidential pardon,

00:40:56.110 --> 00:40:58.930
it really appears that
this a backdoor pardon

00:40:58.930 --> 00:41:00.420
by the Department of Justice,

00:41:00.420 --> 00:41:04.030
that instead of making
President Trump take the fallout

00:41:04.030 --> 00:41:05.530
from actually pardoning

00:41:05.530 --> 00:41:08.530
a sentenced and convicted Michael Flynn,

00:41:08.530 --> 00:41:10.380
they're not even going
to get to that stage

00:41:10.380 --> 00:41:13.330
by dismissing the investigation entirely

00:41:13.330 --> 00:41:14.740
without even getting to sentencing;

00:41:14.740 --> 00:41:16.540
so it was like the plea never happened.

00:41:16.540 --> 00:41:17.373
